(
    title: "3-D Tic-Tac-Toe",
    developer: Some("Carol Shaw"),
    description: Some("Noughts-and-crosses expanded to a 4×4×4 cube, shown as four stacked 4×4 grids. You win by claiming four squares that form a straight line — within one grid, straight up through all four levels, or along any diagonal that runs through the stack — which makes both attack and defence far harder to read than the flat game. You can play a second person or the console itself, whose skill runs across eight levels of look-ahead, the highest taking a very long time to move."),
